{"parse": {"title": "Gone Girl", "pageid": 40658934, "redirects": [], "text": {"*": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Gone Girl</b> may refer to:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Gone_Girl_(album)\" title=\"Gone Girl (album)\"><i>Gone Girl</i> (album)</a>, a 1978 album by Johnny Cash\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Gone_Girl_(Johnny_Cash_song)\" title=\"Gone Girl (Johnny Cash song)\">\"Gone Girl\" (Johnny Cash song)</a> from the album by Johnny Cash</li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Gone_Girl_(Iann_Dior_song)\" title=\"Gone Girl (Iann Dior song)\">\"Gone Girl\" (Iann Dior song)</a>, 2019</li>\n<li>\"Gone Girl\", a song by SZA from the 2022 album <i><a href=\"/wiki/SOS_(SZA_album)\" title=\"SOS (SZA album)\">SOS</a></i></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Gone_Girl_(novel)\" title=\"Gone Girl (novel)\"><i>Gone Girl</i> (novel)</a>, a 2012 thriller novel by Gillian Flynn\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Gone_Girl_(film)\" title=\"Gone Girl (film)\"><i>Gone Girl</i> (film)</a>, a 2014 film based on the novel, directed by David Fincher\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Gone_Girl_(soundtrack)\" title=\"Gone Girl (soundtrack)\"><i>Gone Girl</i> (soundtrack)</a>, a soundtrack album for the 2014 film</li></ul></li></ul></li>\n<li>\"Gone Girl\", a short story written by <a href=\"/wiki/Ross_Macdonald\" title=\"Ross Macdonald\">Ross Macdonald</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Gone_Girl_(The_Vampire_Diaries)\" title=\"Gone Girl (The Vampire Diaries)\">\"Gone Girl\" (<i>The Vampire Diaries</i>)</a>, an episode of the TV series <i>The Vampire Diaries</i> which first aired in 2014</li>\n<li>Gone Girl (Katie Sawyer), a Marvel Comics character and member of <a href=\"/wiki/X-Statix\" title=\"X-Statix\">X-Statix</a></li>\n<li><i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Real_Gone_Girls\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"The Real Gone Girls\">The Real Gone Girls</a></i>, a 1970 film based on the 1965 novel of the same name, directed by James Hill</li>\n<li>A kidnapping committed by <a href=\"/wiki/Matthew_Muller\" title=\"Matthew Muller\">Matthew Muller</a> initially believed to be a hoax was referred to as the \"Gone Girl\" kidnapping</li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"See_also\">See also</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=Gone_Girl&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Girls_Gone_By_Publishers\" title=\"Girls Gone By Publishers\">Girls Gone By Publishers</a>, a UK publisher</li></ul>\n<div class=\"shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux\" style=\"display:none\">Topics referred to by the same term</div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1374546851\">.mw-parser-output .dmbox{display:flex;align-items:center;clear:both;margin:0.9em 1em;border-top:1px solid var(--border-color-subtle,#c8ccd1);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color-subtle,#c8ccd1);padding:0.25em 0.35em;font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output .dmbox>*{flex-shrink:0;margin:0 0.25em}.mw-parser-output .dmbox-body{flex-grow:1;flex-shrink:1;padding:0.1em 0}.mw-parser-output .dmbox-invalid-type{text-align:center}</style>\n<div role=\"note\" id=\"disambigbox\" class=\"metadata plainlinks dmbox dmbox-disambig\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Disambig_gray.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img alt=\"Disambiguation icon\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5f/Disambig_gray.svg/40px-Disambig_gray.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5f/Disambig_gray.svg/60px-Disambig_gray.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"220\" data-file-height=\"168\" /></a></span><div class=\"dmbo